# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values. `.env*` is ignored by
# git on purpose, so the real file never lands in a commit — this one is the
# template that shows up in the repo.
#
# Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables, same names, keep the
# NEXT_PUBLIC prefix (the browser reads them). Redeploy afterwards — these are
# inlined at build time, not read at runtime.
#
# With both keys present the client in src/lib/supabase.ts exists and the forms
# in src/components/AuthPanel.tsx are live. Without them the app still runs and
# the account pages say the cloud is not connected.

# --- Supabase: Project Settings → API --------------------------------------
# "Project URL" and the anon key, which is now sometimes labelled "Publishable
# key". Both are meant to be public; the row policies are what protect the data.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# --- OAuth -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing OAuth-related belongs in this file. Supabase is the broker and holds
# the client secrets; the browser only ever sees the anon key above.
#
# 1. The callback URI you register with each provider is always
#    https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#      Google: https://console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials
#        → OAuth client ID (Web application); JS origins = your site and
#        http://localhost:3000; redirect URI = the Supabase callback above.
#      GitHub: https://github.com/settings/developers → OAuth Apps → New OAuth
#        App; homepage = your site; callback = the Supabase callback above.
#    Paste the id and secret into Supabase → Authentication → Providers.
#
# 2. Your own domain goes in Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration →
#    Redirect URLs, not in the providers:
#      https://glyph.lordpipon.com/**
#      http://localhost:3000/**
#    and Site URL = https://glyph.lordpipon.com. Sign-in sends the reader to
#    /auth/callback, which only exists to close the popup.
